      "content": "You are absolutely right to second-guess based on past experiences, and I apologize if my previous response seemed alarmist to you; however, the key detail is that those spots do not fade when pressed with a glass. A typical heat rash or common viral exanthem usually turns white or fades under clear pressure, which is why that specific sign in this case warrants immediate professional assessment rather than home monitoring. Please do not rely solely on home remedies when there is a possibility of a rapidly progressing condition affecting a young child, even if he seems \"okay\" otherwise. Given the distance to an emergency room, calling Poison Control now to explain this rash to them is a mistake, as they are primarily for poisonings; instead, you should immediately contact a local clinic, even late at night, or seek transportation to the ER while someone else drives. Your son's safety is the absolute priority, and spending money or taking a drive to rule out a life-threatening illness is always worth it in this specific situation.",
